## Parent

omp-plugins-4nv

## What to build

pstack settings join the Root Plugin Configuration as a `behavior.pstack` section:
- suspend Caveman;
- suspend Ponytail;
- maximum panel size, 1–5;
- guard strictness.

The `/omp-plugins` dialog gains a pstack page that follows ADR-0004:
- edits are staged as a draft, and Apply emits the config-changed event;
- running sessions pick up the change live;
- a missing plugin is reported;
- the page links to `/pstack setup`.

`/pstack doctor` reports:
- role coverage;
- panel rules (duplicate model, single vendor);
- skill-name ownership for every workflow-called skill;
- Instruction Mode suspension wiring;
- Display Host availability;
- whether task isolation is enabled.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Changing a pstack setting and applying it updates running pstack behavior without a restart.
- [ ] With the pstack plugin absent, the page shows it as not installed.
- [ ] Doctor flags a duplicate seat model, a single-vendor panel, a workflow-called skill name owned by another source, disabled task isolation, and a missing Display Host. Each check has a harness test.
- [ ] The root settings tests are extended for the pstack page (prior art: the existing root settings tests).
